PlotStars←{
   ⍝ ASCII star map - stereographic projection centered on zenith
   ⍝ Size adapts to width ⍺. Matches book example layout:
   ⍝ horizon circle, crosshairs, cardinal directions, planet labels
    margin←4
    cols←⍺-2×margin
    rows←1+⌊cols÷2
    cr←1+⌊rows÷2 ⋄ cc←1+⌊cols÷2
    rr←⌊(rows-3)÷2 ⋄ rc←⌊(cols-3)÷2
    row←{⌊0.5+cr-rr×⍵[;2]} ⋄ col←{⌊0.5+cc+rc×⍵[;1]}
    inside←{(⍺≥1)∧(⍺≤rows)∧(⍵≥1)∧⍵≤cols}
   ⍝ Crosshairs
    grid←rows cols⍴' '
    grid[cr;]←'─' ⋄ grid[;cc]←'│' ⋄ grid[cr;cc]←'┼'
   ⍝ Horizon circle (360 points)
    a←(⍳360)×(○2)÷360
    hr←1⌈rows⌊⌊0.5+cr-rr×2○a
    hc←1⌈cols⌊⌊0.5+cc+rc×1○a
    grid←(⍴grid)⍴'·'@(∪((hr-1)×cols)+hc)⊢,grid
   ⍝ Cardinal directions, then scale mark, where they fit
    marks←((cr-rr-1)cc)((cr+rr+1)cc)(cr(cc-rc-1))(cr(cc+rc+1))
    fit←{⊃inside/⍵}¨marks
    grid←(fit/'NSEW')@(fit/marks)⊢grid
    scale←(cc-rc-4)+⍳3
    grid[cr;(1≤cc-rc-4)/scale]←(1≤cc-rc-4)/'1.0'
   ⍝ Stars: bright *, faint .; each cell takes the first star to reach it,
   ⍝ unless it already holds something other than space or crosshair
    stars←⍵.StarCoord
    sr←row stars ⋄ sc←col stars
    in←sr inside sc
    cell←in/((sr-1)×cols)+sc
    symbol←in/'.*'[1+⍵.StarsVisible/Data.BRIGHT]
    put←(≠cell)∧(,grid)[cell]∊' ─│'
    grid←(⍴grid)⍴(put/symbol)@(put/cell)⊢,grid
   ⍝ Planets, in order: symbol, and name label to the right if room
    vp←⍵.PlanetsVisible
    symbols←vp/(≢vp)↑'☾☉☿♀♂♃♄⛢♆♇☄'
    names←vp/(≢vp)↑Data.PLANETNAMES
    pr←row ⍵.PlanetCoord ⋄ pc←col ⍵.PlanetCoord
    place←{
        r c symbol name←⍺
        g←⍵ ⋄ g[r;c]←symbol
        label←' ',name
        cols<c+≢label: g
        ~∧/g[r;c+⍳≢label]∊' ─│┼': g
        g[r;c+⍳≢label]←label ⋄ g
    }
    grid←⊃place/(⌽(pr inside pc)/pr,¨pc,¨symbols,¨⊂¨names),⊂grid
   ⍝ Output with margin, then key
    pad←margin⍴' '
    z←(pad∘,¨↓grid),'' (pad,'  * bright   . faint   ┼ zenith   · horizon')
    ~∨/vp: z
    z,⊂pad,' ',∊' ',¨symbols,¨'=',¨names }
